While the operation is in progress, checkout --merge rebuilds the
conflict from HEAD/MERGE_HEAD/merge-base, so it discards a staged
resolution too — not just unstaged edits. (Once the operation ends and
those refs are gone, there is nothing left to rebuild from.)

Erik noted this also discards a staged rerere result. It does — but it
discards the *applied* resolution only; the recorded preimage in
.git/rr-cache survives (git rerere forget is the explicit way to drop
that). I chose not to add a rerere caveat to section 6: keeping a botched
resolution discardable while the recording survives is the behavior we
want, and the line would have added noise for an edge case.

The :/ pathspec is the "top" magic signature (anchored at the repo
root). I picked it over . deliberately so the restart reaches conflicted
files in sibling directories regardless of cwd.

Version bump is a patch. It is arguably minor since it removes guidance
and redirects to a different command, but it reads as a scope correction
rather than new behavior, and Erik picked patch when asked.

The working tree has unrelated untracked files (analyze_tool_costs.py,
read_transcripts.py, issues/, a workspace dir). This commit stages only
the two skill files.
